        {
          "post_id": "491098",
          "text": "<p>Which two of the following four regular expressions are equivalent? ($\\varepsilon$ is the empty string).<br><br>i. $0^* 1(0+1)^*$<br><br>ii. $(0+1)^* 10^*$<br><br>iii. $0^* 1^* 0^*$<br><br>iv. $(0+1)^* 1(0+1)^*$<br>(Select all that apply.)</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>(i) and (ii)<br>&nbsp;</li><li>(i) and (iv)<br>&nbsp;</li><li>(ii) and (iii)<br>&nbsp;</li><li>(iii) and (iv)</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "A;B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "subject": "Theory of Computation",
          "day": "Day 105"
        },
        {
          "post_id": "491095",
          "text": "<p>Let $w$ be any string of length $n&gt;1$ over the alphabet $\\{0,1\\}^*$. Let $L_p$ be the set of all nonempty prefixes of $w$ and $L_s$ be the set of all non-empty suffixes of $w$.</p><p>Consider the language $L$ formed by the concatenation of these two sets: $L=L_p \\cdot L_s=\\{u v \\mid u \\in L_p$ and $\\left.v \\in L_s\\right\\}$.</p><p>What is the minimum number of states in a non-deterministic finite automaton (NFA) that accepts the language $L$ ?</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$n+1$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$2 n$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$2 n+1$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$n^2$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "C",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "subject": "Theory of Computation",
          "day": "Day 105"
        },
        {
          "post_id": "491090",
          "text": "<p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><b id=\"docs-internal-guid-5ceeb508-7fff-9047-4a83-b766e033b624\"><img width=\"372\" height=\"226\" alt=\"\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></b></p><p>The language accepted by this automaton is given by the regular expression</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$\\left(b^* a\\left(a b^* a\\right)^* b+\\varepsilon\\right)(a+b b)^*$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$(a+b)^*$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$b^* a(a+b)^* b(a+b b)^*$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$(a+b b)^*$</li></ol>",
