        {
          "post_id": "491089",
          "text": "<p>Consider the following context-free grammar $G$ with start variable $S$ and terminals $a, b$:</p><p>$$<br>S \\rightarrow a S b|S S| a b<br>$$</p><p><br>Which ONE of the following languages is generated by $G$ ?</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$L(G)=\\left\\{w \\in\\{a, b\\}^{+} \\mid n_a(w)=n_b(w)\\right.$ and for every prefix $p$ of $\\left.w, n_a(p) \\geq n_b(p)\\right\\}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$L(G)=\\left\\{w \\in\\{a, b\\}^{+} \\mid n_a(w)=n_b(w)\\right\\}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$L(G)=\\left\\{a^n b^n \\mid n \\geq 1\\right\\} \\cup\\left\\{(a b)^n \\mid n \\geq 1\\right\\}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$L(G)=\\left\\{w \\in\\{a, b\\}^{+} \\mid\\right.$every $a$ has a matching $b$ somewhere to its right $\\}$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "subject": "Theory of Computation",
          "day": "Day 105"
        },
        {
          "post_id": "491081",
          "text": "<p>Consider the following context-free grammar: $G$, where $S, A$, and $B$ are the variables (nonterminals), $a, b, c$, and $d$ are the terminal symbols, $S$ is the start variable, and the rules of $G$ are described as:</p><p>$$<br>\\begin{aligned}<br>& S \\rightarrow A \\mid B \\\\<br>& A \\rightarrow a A b b \\mid a b b \\\\<br>& B \\rightarrow c c B d \\mid c c d<br>\\end{aligned}<br>$$</p><p><br>Which ONE of the following languages $L(G)$ is generated by $G$ ?</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$L(G)=\\left\\{a^n b^{2 n} \\mid n \\geq 1\\right\\} \\cup\\left\\{c^{2 m} d^m \\mid m \\geq 1\\right\\}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$L(G)=\\left\\{a^{2 n} b^n \\mid n \\geq 1\\right\\} \\cup\\left\\{c^m d^{2 m} \\mid m \\geq 1\\right\\}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$L(G)=\\left\\{a^n b^n \\mid n \\geq 1\\right\\} \\cup\\left\\{c^m d^m \\mid m \\geq 1\\right\\}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$L(G)=\\left\\{a^n b^{2 n} c^{2 m} d^m \\mid n \\geq 1, m \\geq 1\\right\\}$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "A",
